cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Regulon in coursework, a tutorial, a talk, or your own project,
  a citation or a link back is appreciated but never required — this project
  is free to learn from and build on under the MIT license.
title: Regulon
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Shake MD Tareq
    family-names: Hasan
    alias: shakehasan
repository-code: "https://github.com/shakehasan/regulon"
abstract: >-
  An open-source, local-first reference platform for governed multi-agent
  RAG: LangGraph orchestration, hybrid retrieval with citations, layered
  routing, RBAC, hash-chained audit trails, human-in-the-loop approval, and
  evaluation-gated CI. Built as a free learning resource for the GitHub
  community; no accounts, API keys, or paid services required to run it.
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-07-02
